Scenario A transfer entered from the other account is a duplicate in this one
Description The movement is already in this account's register. It was entered
\ against the joint account, naming Ken Checking as its other side, so
\ Ken Checking shows it as a deposit without owning a row of its own.
\ Reading Ken Checking's own statement reaches that same movement.
Details Nothing is brought up to date on a duplicate found this way. The
\ cleared marker and the identifier both belong to the account the
\ transaction lives in, and this file is not that account's bank
\ speaking, so the transaction is left exactly as it is and the row is
\ reported as a duplicate. See what a duplicate does to the transaction
\ already there.
\ The other half of a payment is a different thing and is still New.
\ There the book holds the other account's own row, whose other side is
\ nobody yet, and no transaction names this account at all -- so this
\ account's register has no line for the money and the row is the first
\ of them. See a half already in the book is found on the amount and
\ the date.
Given the chart of accounts is : ChartOfAccounts
| Path                   | Type     | Placeholder |
| Assets:Joint Checking  | Checking | false       |
| Assets:Ken Checking    | Checking | false       |
| Expenses:Uncategorized | Expense  | false       |
And transactions are : ImportedTransaction
| Ref | SourceAccount         | Date       | Payee           | Destination         | Amount   | Cleared | FitId       |
| T1  | Assets:Joint Checking | 2026-09-30 | TO KEN CHECKING | Assets:Ken Checking | -3000.00 | Cleared | 20260930001 |
And import target is : ImportTarget Vertical
| AccountPath | Assets:Ken Checking |
When transactions imported : OfxTransactions
| TrnType | DatePosted | Amount  | FitId       | Name               | Memo | CheckNum |
| CREDIT  | 2026-09-30 | 3000.00 | 20260930777 | TRANSFER FROM 3105 | none | none     |
Then import summary is : ImportSummary Vertical
| New       | 0 |
| Duplicate | 1 |
| Possible  | 0 |
And transactions are : ImportedTransaction
| Ref | SourceAccount         | Date       | Payee           | Destination         | Amount   | Cleared | FitId       |
| T1  | Assets:Joint Checking | 2026-09-30 | TO KEN CHECKING | Assets:Ken Checking | -3000.00 | Cleared | 20260930001 |
# One transaction, untouched: it keeps the identifier the joint account's own
# download gave it and does not take this one. In Ken Checking's register the
# line reads 3000.00 the other way up, which is what the row says.

Scenario Two identical downloaded transactions both import
Description A shop visited twice in one day for the same amount gives two
\ transactions with two FITIDs. Each is matched on its own identifier,
\ so neither is mistaken for the other.
